05746"},{"label":"David","color":"#B07CD4"},{"label":"New covenant","color":"#E4DFCE"},{"label":"Unassigned","color":"#5A6178"}],"relkinds":[{"key":"quoted-in","label":"Quoted in","color":"#E8C15A","strong":true},{"key":"fulfilled-in","label":"Fulfilled in","color":"#D9715C","strong":true},{"key":"parallels","label":"Parallels","color":"#6E9BD1","strong":false},{"key":"illustrates-doctrine","label":"Illustrates doctrine","color":"#9B8AD1","strong":false},{"key":"part-of-covenant","label":"Part of covenant","color":"#5FBFA0","strong":false}],"counts":{"topics":5,"portals":0,"edges":4,"relations":0,"outbound":0},"nodes":[{"id":"bt_book_zep","p":0,"x":56,"y":109,"s":-1,"g":6,"bk":"ZEP","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"Zephaniah: overview","d":"The word of the LORD to Zephaniah in the days of Josiah: the great day of the LORD on Judah and the earth, a call to seek the LORD, judgment on nations and Jerusalem, and promised joy for a humble remnant.","q":"Can {{name}} outline Zephaniah and say what the 'day of the LORD' is in this book?","ev":["Say when the word came (1:1)","Outline: judgment (1), call and nations (2), Jerusalem and remnant (3)"],"pp":[[35,1,1,18],[35,2,1,15],[35,3,1,20]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_zep_day_of_lord_judah","p":0,"x":56,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"ZEP","ty":"THEME","t":"The great day of the LORD on Judah","d":"The LORD says he will sweep away everything, stretching his hand against Judah and Jerusalem for Baal worship, mixed oaths and indifference; the day is near, a day of wrath and darkness that silver and gold cannot buy off.","q":"Can {{name}} describe the day of the LORD in Zephaniah 1 and why it comes on Judah?","ev":["List the sins named in 1:4-6 and 1:12","Describe the day in 1:14-18"],"pp":[[35,1,1,18]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_zep_seek_lord_nations","p":0,"x":244,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"ZEP","ty":"THEME","t":"Seek the LORD; the nations judged","d":"Zephaniah calls the meek of the earth to seek the LORD, righteousness and meekness, perhaps to be hidden in the day of anger; he announces judgment on Philistia, Moab, Ammon, Ethiopia and Assyria's Nineveh, with a place left for Judah's remnant.","q":"Can {{name}} say what Zephaniah 2:3 tells the meek to do and which nations are judged in the chapter?","ev":["Read 2:3","List the nations and what is said of each","Say who gains the coast in 2:7"],"pp":[[35,2,1,15]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_zep_jerusalem_judged","p":0,"x":56,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"ZEP","ty":"THEME","t":"The oppressing city and the LORD within","d":"Jerusalem is condemned as filthy and oppressing: she did not listen or trust the LORD, and her princes, judges, prophets and priests are corrupt, though the just LORD in her midst does no iniquity, and the LORD tells them to wait until he gathers the nations.","q":"Can {{name}} explain how Zephaniah 3:1-8 describes Jerusalem's leaders and the LORD in her midst?","ev":["List who is charged in 3:3-4","Say what the LORD hoped for in 3:7"],"pp":[[35,3,1,8]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_zep_the_lord_rejoices_over_you","p":0,"x":244,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"ZEP","ty":"THEME","t":"The remnant restored; the LORD sings over you","d":"The LORD promises to purify the speech of the peoples, leave a humble remnant who trust in him, and cause Zion to sing, for the LORD their king is in her midst, mighty to save, rejoicing over her with singing, and gathering the outcast.","q":"Can {{name}} describe what Zephaniah 3:17 says the LORD does over his people?","ev":["Describe the remnant in 3:12-13","Read 3:17 and say what the LORD does for his people"],"pp":[[35,3,9,20]],"tier":null}],"edges":[[1,0,0],[2,1,1],[3,2,0],[4,3,1]],"rel":[]}
